WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.760
Good morning, Hank. It’s Tuesday. It's Question Tuesday, the day that I answer real questions from real nerdfighters.

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:05.440
Let’s get right to it.

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:07.520
How is the world going to end?

00:00:07.529 --> 00:00:08.830
I’m glad we’re starting on a light note.

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:12.880
So, for the last couple years, I’ve been
thinking a lot about this weird reptile species tuatara.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:14.560
I’ve actually got a tuatara on the wall
back there.

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:20.260
One of the things that gets me about tuatara is that they’ve been on Earth over 150 million years.

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:28.440
Humans, meanwhile, emerged like maybe 300,000 years ago, so we’ve been for at most 0.2% of tuatara history.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:34.820
What I’m getting at is that I kind of suspect that our world may end a long time before the world.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:38.680
As for how, I’m with T.S. Eliot on that one: “Not with a bang, but with a whimper.”

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:40.600
So what’s even the point of getting out
of bed?

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:44.500
Okay, I think the point of getting out of
bed is to seek a reason to get out of bed.

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:52.640
And I know that’s kind of a recursive answer to your question, but I don’t think we can expect, like, fulfillment and meaning to like descend upon us miraculously.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:56.360
I think meaning is something we make together, and that’s what gets me out of bed in the morning.

00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:58.520
Or at the latest, in the early afternoon.

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:00.180
Where did you write Turtles All the Way Down?

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:04.160
Mostly in bed, now that I think of it. I’m not great at following my own advice.

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:07.120
The internet makes me feel worse, but I can’t stop using it question mark?

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:11.320
Yeah. Yeah. I do think there are some pockets of the internet that make us feel better,

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:19.700
but due to some issues with the wiring of the human brain and also the architecture of the social internet, it is difficult, at least for me, to spend a lot of time in those places.

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:21.100
I actually have the same problem with food.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:27.700
Like, I could eat the stuff that makes me
feel good, but some considerable portion of me seems to want to not feel good.

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:31.060
That’s not really an answer to your question, it’s just an expression of commiseration.

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:32.860
Are you still mad that pennies exist?

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:35.160
I wouldn’t say mad so much as disappointed.

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:37.900
Are you dreading or looking forward to the book tour?

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:42.620
I am so looking forward to it. I can’t even tell you how much joy it brings me to be on tour with Hank.

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:43.820
Don’t tell him I said that.

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:47.120
Hey, what cities on the Turtles tour are sold out or close to being sold out?

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:49.900
The shows in Bellingham, Chicago, and Atlanta are sold out.

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:51.220
I’m sorry that happened so quickly.

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:54.060
A number of other places are close, so now is a good time to get tickets.

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:55.820
Here are all the cities we will be visiting.

00:01:55.820 --> 00:01:59.800
More info and tickets at turtlesallthewaydownbook.com. Link in the dooblydoo.

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:02.260
Is it rude if I come to your book tour mostly to see Hank?

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:03.710
No, why do you think I’m going?

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:05.240
Vulcans or Klingons?

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:07.399
For me, that’s more of an “and” than
an “or.”

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:09.020
Vulcans AND Klingons.

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:10.140
Coffee or tea?

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:11.740
Again, I’m gonna go with and.

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:13.860
How do you feel about animals with no necks?

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:17.660
Oh, no. No, no, no. Profoundly disturbing. Undo, undo!

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:20.700
If you could live in any time besides this
one, what would it be?

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:25.960
Probably just the time like right before I
found out about the corner of the internet devoted to animals with no necks.

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:27.440
Best hotdog you ever consumed?

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:30.592
Once in Reykjavik, Iceland, I went to this
hotdog stand and the hotdogs were like a dollar,

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:36.580
and it wasn’t just the best hotdog I’ve
ever eaten, it was like one of the two or three best meals I’ve ever eaten.

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:40.960
I know this wouldn’t surprise Freud, but
I literally sometimes dream about that hotdog.

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:43.290
Who’s your least favorite American founding father?

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:50.140
James Wilkinson was like an actual secret agent working against the United States, but even so, I think you could make a case for Aaron Burr.

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:53.600
Is Turtles All the Way Down going to be translated into Spanish and/or other languages?

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:55.460
Yes. In fact, here is the Spanish cover.

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:57.820
Do you ever feel like something you finished isn’t good enough.

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:02.600
Yes, I feel that way every Tuesday evening
and then once every 3 to 6 years when I publish a new book.

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:07.740
Like, if you’re writing a book, the goal
is to use language to create an experience inside of someone else’s mind, right?

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:12.000
And I think there will always be failures
in that, partly because of your own insufficiencies.

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:17.520
You’re always gonna run up against the limits of your talent, but also partly because of the insufficiencies of language itself.

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:19.920
I think it’s the same with building something in the physical world.

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:23.460
Like, both the wood and the carpenter will
always have their imperfections.

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:30.060
So, inevitably, all buildings will fall short
of the way they’re initially imagined, but even so, they can provide us shelter.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:31.940
Hank, congratulations on a great VidCon Australia.

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:36.460
I hope you’re getting some rest because
we go on tour in just 27 days!

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:38.460
But before then, I will see you on Friday.

